      "en": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "He extends the reward for mitzvos that a person does for two thousand generations (for the benefit of his descendants)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 0
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "He forgives deliberate sins."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 1
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "He forgives rebellious sins."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 2
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "He forgives unintentional sins."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 3
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "He cleanses those who do teshuvah and gives them a fresh start!"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 4
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Please forgive our sins—and keep us as Your special and eternal nation—for You are full of kindness to all who call to You."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 5
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of those who will be able earn a living and have their material needs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of merits. (See Instant Insight below.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of those who will be pardoned and forgiven."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us and ensure we earn a living and have our material needs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us for merits. (See Instant Insight below.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us and pardon and forgive us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, let our salvation come very soon!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, raise up high the honor of Your nation Bnei Yisrael."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, raise up high the honor of the Mashiach."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, fill up our hands with Your blessings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, fill our storehouses with abundance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, hear our voice, spare us and have compassion on us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, accept our tefillos with compassion and favor."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "_legacySource": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "subsection",
      "he": "",
      "en": "A SPECIAL TIME, SPECIAL REQUESTS"
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "On fast days (except Tishah B'Av) and during the Aseres Yemei Teshuvah, we add Avinu Malkeinu before Tachanun:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "note"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "NOTE: The Hebrew of this tefillah is quite simple and straightforward. I urge you to say each line slowly in the original."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(During Aseres Yemei Teshuvah say:)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(On fast days say:)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "note"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(The following nine are said responsively—first by the chazzan:)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "note"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The following five are said during Aseres Yemei Teshuvah:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "note"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The following five are said on fast days:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "instant_insight",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Regarding the \"book of merits\" or remembering us \"for merits\": Either one has merits or they do not! If they do, they are in the book; and if not, what is Hashem supposed to do? What does this mean? The idea here is that Hashem could arrange your life so that it's easy for you to pick up merits and good deeds (someone in front of you drops something and you pick it up!) or the opposite—you simply do not have easy opportunities to do good deeds. We are asking Hashem to please remember us and write us in the book of those who will have many opportunities to do mitzvos!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}